<title>USA: Positron sees liquidity problems CEO quits.</title>
<headline>Positron sees liquidity problems CEO quits.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Positron Corp said on Friday that its chief executive has resigned, the company is having liquidity problems and its outside auditors have substantial doubts that it can continue as a going concern.</p>
<p>Positron reported a fourth-quarter loss of $0.41 per share, and a full-year 1996 loss of $6.4 million, or $1.67 per share, including $1.8 million in non-recurring losses from problems with its international installations.</p>
<p>The company said its president and chief executive, Werner Haas, has resigned.  His duties have been taken on by the chairman, Gary Wood.</p>
</text>
